# Farokhi et al. 2023, Fig. 2/Fig. 3: 90 MeV proton, 21 % O2.
# Molar value is the paper's own Henry's-law conversion at 37 C
# (not the project's % shortcut, which assumes a different constant).
#
# halfBox 5 um -> a 10x10x10 um^3 box, matching the paper's own "sensitive
# volume" (Fig. 1B) directly, rather than the project's 500 um default: at
# 90 MeV the proton's LET (~0.57 keV/um) is constant either way, but the
# default 1 mm box deposits ~570 keV along the track, and the full IRT
# particle-based stage (no mesoscopic hand-over) does not scale to that many
# radiolytic species -- 40-70+ min per event, infeasible for /run/beamOn 20.
# At 10 um the deposit drops to ~6 keV, back to a tractable IRT cost; the
# trade-off is that rare, longer-range secondary electrons (max delta-ray
# range ~0.3-0.4 mm at this energy) are truncated at the box edge instead of
# depositing their full energy, same caveat the paper itself accepts with its
# own 10 um sensitive volume.

/run/verbose 0
/tracking/verbose 0
/dnaLogger/verbose Info

/process/dna/e-SolvationSubType Ritchie1994

/chem/select Farokhi2023
/chem/meso/enable false
/chem/env/halfBox 5 um

/chem/env/scavenger O2 218 uM

/run/initialize

/scheduler/endTime 1 us

/gun/particle proton
/gun/energy 90 MeV

/run/beamOn 20
/run/dumpDataAndReset
